Z||000009||Fformula88||09-26-2001||12:17 PM||||I'd recommend you take the car somewhere else for a second opinion!<P>Most car dealers service departments are untrutworthy at best and fraudulent at worst!  Some of the things I have heard about from mechanics would make you wonder why anybody would take their car there.  <P>Anyway, I'd be skeptical that they just think they can sucker you into a new engine since you brought in an old car.  Talk to some people and find a good priate mechanic.  (no chain places either!)<P>I am curious to the complete symptoms of the car... and if it has had an engine light or not.  Could be a lot of things causing the problem.<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||09-26-2001||02:59 PM||||gas in the oil could simply be from being flooded or an injector stuck open. Def get another opinion.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||09-26-2001||03:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by dennis_6:<BR><B>Dealership said there is gas in the oil and that I need another engine.   </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> Gas in the oil doesn't necessarily mean you need a new engine. Yeesh!!<BR>Sounds like it was severely flooded at one time, but that normally won't kill an engine.<P>Get a *written* diagnosis from where it is now. (You're paying them for this, right?) <BR>Then take it someplace else. <BR>Once you get it fixed, have these shysters prosecuted for trying to defraud you. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||8
